  "findings": [
    "All six runs retained their complete declared process set: point_cloud_preprocessor_node plus scan_to_map_odometry_node for custom, and rtabmap for RTAB-Map.",
    "Custom full-stack mean CPU was 22.16% [22.00, 22.67], 1.33x RTAB-Map's 16.62% [16.04, 17.08]. Their sampled peak CPU was nearly equal: median 44.98% for both.",
    "Custom final RSS was 454.7 MiB [454.1, 454.8], 53.7% of RTAB-Map's 846.3 MiB [837.3, 849.9]. RTAB-Map additionally wrote a 60.5-60.6 MiB database.",
    "The corrected custom RSS is about 112 MiB above the superseded matcher-only measurement, confirming that omission of the preprocessor was material.",
    "Across this batch RTAB-Map position RMSE varied from 0.0325 to 0.0500 m while custom remained 0.0113 m. Combining this independent batch with the previous three runs expands the observed RTAB-Map/custom position-RMSE ratio from 2.25-2.87x to 2.25-4.43x."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Three runs per stack are an observed range, not a confidence interval.",
    "The stacks were run sequentially at 1.0x on the same host and input. Host load was not externally pinned or isolated at the operating-system scheduler level.",
    "CPU is aggregate process CPU and may exceed 100% for multi-threaded workloads. Peak RSS is the maximum simultaneously sampled sum, not a sum of per-process peaks.",
    "Disk bytes and resident memory are reported separately and must not be added as though they were the same resource.",
    "The comparison remains specific to one closed two-lap trajectory and the shipped configurations."
  ],
  "method": "Three sequential 1.0x replays per stack through map_projection_comparison.launch.py. Process identity was matched only against argv[0]; ambiguous, missing or lost processes invalidate a resource row. Every trajectory consumed the byte-identical bag and recorded odometry.",
